    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe business-day rule for the registration date now extends to public holidays. In `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`, the `rollToBusinessDay` method previously only advanced weekend dates to the following Monday. I updated it so that:\n\n1. **Added the fixed holiday calendar** as a `Set<LocalDate>` constant `PUBLIC_HOLIDAYS`: 2026-01-01, 2026-01-26, 2026-04-25, 2026-12-25, 2026-12-28.\n\n2. **Rewrote `rollToBusinessDay`** to loop, advancing one day at a time while the date is either a weekend or a listed holiday, until it lands on a non-holiday business day. The loop is necessary because rolling off a weekend can land on a holiday and vice versa (e.g. Fri 2026-12-25 holiday \u2192 weekend Sat/Sun \u2192 Mon 2026-12-28 holiday \u2192 Tue 2026-12-29).\n\n3. **Extracted an `isWeekend` helper** to keep the weekend check readable, preserving the original `switch`-on-`DayOfWeek` idiom.\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest.coreDefaultDateIsBusinessDay` invariant (default registration date is never Saturday/Sunday) passes, and `BUILD SUCCESS` for the full suite (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).",
